1lgp|n|Pleasing by delicacy or grace; attracting, but not striking or impressing; of a pleasing and attractive form a color; having slight or diminutive beauty; neat or elegant without elevation or grandeur; pleasingly, but not grandly, conceived or expressed; as, a pretty face; a pretty flower; a pretty poem. ; Moderately large; considerable; as, he had saved a pretty fortune. ; Affectedly nice; foppish; -- used in an ill sense. ; Mean; despicable; contemptible; -- used ironically; as, a pretty trick; a pretty fellow. ; Stout; strong and brave; intrepid; valiant.	V:hoh,52,2;108x,22,2;nmr,10,1;fhw,4,1;14yz,1,1~108x,22,2;hoh,52,2;14yz,1,1;fhw,4,1;nmr,10,1	N:1hco,62,3;hrv,26,1;7yd,11,1~1hco,62,3;hrv,26,1;7yd,11,1
