1m36|a|Belonging to one; one's own; individual. ; Belonging to the natural or essential constitution; peculiar; not common; particular; as, every animal has his proper instincts and appetites. ; Befitting one's nature, qualities, etc.; suitable in all respect; appropriate; right; fit; decent; as, water is the proper element for fish; a proper dress. ; Becoming in appearance; well formed; handsome. ; Pertaining to one of a species, but not common to the whole; not appellative; -- opposed to common; as, a proper name; Dublin is the proper name of a city. ; Rightly so called; strictly considered; as, Greece proper; the garden proper. ; Represented in its natural color; -- said of any object used as a charge.	j:26xs,74,11;1rt3,66,4;1d10,62,4;vt7,62,4;5e5,61,3;1y71,59,7;1muz,55,4;5f8,51,14;uba,47,7;5l0,46,5~gjy,25,16;cwu,22,15;5f8,51,14;26xs,74,11;1zml,12,10;vkz,44,9;16f1,13,8;15ht,2,7;asr,8,7;2oo,12,7	e:on4,9,5~on4,9,5
