1m7o|n|The ordinary language of men in speaking or writing; language not cast in poetical measure or rhythm; -- contradistinguished from verse, or metrical composition. ; Hence, language which evinces little imagination or animation; dull and commonplace discourse. ; A hymn with no regular meter, sometimes introduced into the Mass. See Sequence.	a:ocd,44,3;vdr,6,2~ocd,44,3;vdr,6,2	v:29cv,19,1~29cv,19,1
