1mhb|a|Sagacious in adapting means to ends; circumspect in action, or in determining any line of conduct; practically wise; judicious; careful; discreet; sensible; -- opposed to rash; as, a prudent man; dictated or directed by prudence or wise forethought; evincing prudence; as, prudent behavior. ; Frugal; economical; not extravagant; as, a prudent woman; prudent expenditure of money.	e:2cj,23,3;1awf,15,3~1awf,15,3;2cj,23,3
